From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:15:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] kboot: Pass on which touch firmware variant the unit needs

The iPhone X's ADT names the variant of Apple's touch firmware the unit
needs. Copy it through the touchscreen0 alias, so the driver can load the
firmware of that variant.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/kboot.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kboot.c b/src/kboot.c
index 27ebe5e..b3a9639 100644
--- a/src/kboot.c
+++ b/src/kboot.c
@@ -947,6 +947,8 @@ static int dt_set_touchscreen(void)
         {"luna-shape-flex-noise", "apple,luna-shape-flex-noise"},
         {"luna-racer-tmon-comp", "apple,luna-racer-tmon-comp"},
         {"luna-afe-calibration", "apple,luna-afe-calibration"},
+        /* Which firmware variant this unit needs; the driver loads that one. */
+        {"hid-merge-personality", "apple,hid-merge-personality"},
     };
     const char *path = fdt_get_alias(dt, "touchscreen0");
     if (path == NULL)
